  "question": {
    "text": "A particle executes simple harmonic motion between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></math>. If time taken by particle to go from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>; then time taken by particle in going from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0044_c8f941fc6d16.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /></p><p>The position of a particle performing an SHM is given by:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Since at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the particle is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;therefore the initial phase&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>At time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the particle is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Therefore, time period</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p>The total time taken from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p><p>Since the time taken from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, therefore the time taken from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
